#. TRANSLATORS: Initial status bar text
msgid "Ready"
msgstr "Gereed"

#. TRANSLATORS: Startup warning; the placeholder is the error that prevented reopening
msgid "{} — the dictionary was not reopened."
msgstr "{} — het woordenboek is niet opnieuw geopend."

#. TRANSLATORS: Status bar text after opening a dictionary
msgid "Dictionary loaded"
msgstr "Woordenboek geladen"

#. TRANSLATORS: Error shown while exiting; the placeholder is the underlying error
msgid "Could not save session: {}"
msgstr "Kan de sessie niet opslaan: {}"

#. TRANSLATORS: Yes/No question when opening a protected dictionary; the placeholder is the dictionary name
msgid "{} requires a license. Do you want to import a license file now?"
msgstr "{} vereist een licentie. Wil je nu een licentiebestand importeren?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Title of the license question dialog
msgid "License required"
msgstr "Licentie vereist"

#. TRANSLATORS: Error after importing a license that does not unlock the dictionary; the placeholder is the dictionary name
msgid "The imported license does not unlock {}."
msgstr "De geïmporteerde licentie ontgrendelt {} niet."

#. TRANSLATORS: Fallback page title when the entry has no headword
#. TRANSLATORS: Group label around the dictionary article pane
msgid "Article"
msgstr "Artikel"

#. TRANSLATORS: Shown in the article pane when the entry has no content
msgid "Article unavailable."
msgstr "Artikel niet beschikbaar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Announced when a cross-reference target is not in the dictionary; the placeholder is the word
msgid "Not found: {}"
msgstr "Niet gevonden: {}"

#. TRANSLATORS: Title of the error dialog
msgid "Dictymus - Error"
msgstr "Dictymus - Fout"

#. TRANSLATORS: Third-party license notice in the About dialog; the source code links follow on the next lines
msgid "The ASCII braille view uses the louis-rs braille translator and Hebrew braille tables from liblouis, both licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later. Their source code is available at:"
msgstr "De HeBraille-weergave gebruikt de braillevertaler louis-rs en Hebreeuwse brailletabellen van liblouis, beide gelicentieerd onder de GNU Lesser General Public License, versie 2.1 of later. De broncode is beschikbaar op:"

#. TRANSLATORS: One-line app description in the About dialog
msgid "An accessible dictionary for biblical languages"
msgstr "Een toegankelijk woordenboek voor Bijbelse talen"

#. TRANSLATORS: Title of the dictionary file picker dialog
msgid "Open dictionary"
msgstr "Woordenboek openen"

#. TRANSLATORS: File picker filter label for all supported dictionary formats
msgid "Dictionaries (*.dicty;*.ifo;*.mdx)"
msgstr "Woordenboeken (*.dicty;*.ifo;*.mdx)"

#. TRANSLATORS: File picker filter label for Dictymus dictionary containers
msgid "Dictymus dictionaries (*.dicty)"
msgstr "Dictymus-woordenboeken (*.dicty)"

#. TRANSLATORS: File picker filter label for StarDict dictionaries
msgid "StarDict info (*.ifo)"
msgstr "StarDict-info (*.ifo)"

#. TRANSLATORS: File picker filter label for MDict dictionaries
msgid "MDict (*.mdx)"
msgstr "MDict (*.mdx)"

#. TRANSLATORS: File picker filter label for all files
msgid "All files (*.*)"
msgstr "Alle bestanden (*.*)"

#. TRANSLATORS: Title of the license file picker dialog
msgid "Import license"
msgstr "Licentie importeren"

#. TRANSLATORS: File picker filter label for Dictymus license files
msgid "Dictymus licenses (*.dictykey)"
msgstr "Dictymus-licenties (*.dictykey)"

#. TRANSLATORS: Status warning when the bundled SBL BibLit font cannot be registered
msgid "Bundled font could not be registered; using system font"
msgstr "Het meegeleverde lettertype kon niet worden geregistreerd; het systeemlettertype wordt gebruikt"

#. TRANSLATORS: Status warning when the bundled SBL BibLit font cannot be loaded at all
msgid "Bundled font unavailable; using system font"
msgstr "Het meegeleverde lettertype is niet beschikbaar; het systeemlettertype wordt gebruikt"

#. TRANSLATORS: Error shown when the user guide could not be prepared for the web browser
msgid "Could not open the user guide."
msgstr "Kan de handleiding niet openen."

#. TRANSLATORS: Error shown when the web browser could not be started to show the user guide
msgid "Could not start your web browser to show the user guide."
msgstr "Kan je webbrowser niet starten om de handleiding te tonen."

#. TRANSLATORS: Title of the Licenses dialog
msgid "Licenses"
msgstr "Licenties"

#. TRANSLATORS: Label of the list of installed licenses
msgid "Installed &licenses:"
msgstr "Geïnstalleerde &licenties:"

#. TRANSLATORS: Column header in the Licenses dialog: who the license was issued to
msgid "Licensee"
msgstr "Licentiehouder"

#. TRANSLATORS: Column header in the Licenses dialog: license issue date
msgid "Issued"
msgstr "Uitgegeven"

#. TRANSLATORS: Column header in the Licenses dialog: the dictionaries the license unlocks
msgid "Dictionaries"
msgstr "Woordenboeken"

#. TRANSLATORS: Button in the Licenses dialog importing a license file
msgid "&Import..."
msgstr "&Importeren..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Button in the Licenses dialog removing the selected license
msgid "&Remove"
msgstr "Ve&rwijderen"

#. TRANSLATORS: Label of the button closing the Licenses dialog
msgid "Close"
msgstr "Sluiten"

#. TRANSLATORS: Yes/No confirmation before deleting a license; the placeholder is the licensee name
msgid "Remove the license for {}? Dictionaries it unlocks will no longer open."
msgstr "De licentie voor {} verwijderen? Woordenboeken die deze licentie ontgrendelt, kunnen daarna niet meer worden geopend."

#. TRANSLATORS: Title of the remove-license confirmation dialog
msgid "Remove license"
msgstr "Licentie verwijderen"

#. TRANSLATORS: Error installing a license; first placeholder is the file path, second the underlying error
msgid "Cannot read {}: {}"
msgstr "Kan {} niet lezen: {}"

#. TRANSLATORS: Error installing a license file that is invalid or not signed by the publisher
msgid "This is not a valid Dictymus license file."
msgstr "Dit is geen geldig Dictymus-licentiebestand."

#. TRANSLATORS: Error installing a license when no application data directory exists
msgid "No application data directory is available."
msgstr "Er is geen applicatiedatamap beschikbaar."

#. TRANSLATORS: Error installing a license from a path that does not end in a file name
msgid "The license path has no file name."
msgstr "Het licentiepad bevat geen bestandsnaam."

#. TRANSLATORS: Error installing a license; first placeholder is the destination path, second the underlying error
msgid "Cannot install the license to {}: {}"
msgstr "Kan de licentie niet installeren naar {}: {}"

#. TRANSLATORS: Error removing a license; first placeholder is the file path, second the underlying error
msgid "Cannot remove {}: {}"
msgstr "Kan {} niet verwijderen: {}"

msgid "Could not start the single-instance service. Opening dictionary files from Explorer will start a separate window."
msgstr "Kan de service voor een enkele instantie niet starten. Woordenboekbestanden die vanuit de Verkenner worden geopend, starten een apart venster."

#. TRANSLATORS: File menu item; the text after the tab is the keyboard shortcut
msgid "&Open...\tCtrl+O"
msgstr "&Openen...\tCtrl+O"

#. TRANSLATORS: Status bar help for the Open menu item
msgid "Open a dictionary"
msgstr "Een woordenboek openen"

#. TRANSLATORS: File menu item; the text after the tab is the keyboard shortcut
msgid "&Close\tCtrl+F4"
msgstr "&Sluiten\tCtrl+F4"

#. TRANSLATORS: Status bar help for the Close menu item
msgid "Close current dictionary"
msgstr "Het huidige woordenboek sluiten"

#. TRANSLATORS: File menu item
msgid "Close &All"
msgstr "&Alles sluiten"

#. TRANSLATORS: Status bar help for the Close All menu item
msgid "Close all dictionaries"
msgstr "Alle woordenboeken sluiten"

#. TRANSLATORS: File menu item opening the Licenses dialog; the text after the tab is the keyboard shortcut
msgid "&Licenses...\tCtrl+L"
msgstr "&Licenties...\tCtrl+L"

#. TRANSLATORS: Status bar help for the Licenses menu item
msgid "View, import, or remove dictionary licenses"
msgstr "Licenties voor woordenboeken bekijken, importeren of verwijderen"

#. TRANSLATORS: File menu item opening the Options dialog
msgid "&Options..."
msgstr "O&pties..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Status bar help for the Options menu item
msgid "Change settings"
msgstr "Instellingen wijzigen"

#. TRANSLATORS: File menu item; the text after the tab is the keyboard shortcut
msgid "E&xit\tCtrl+Q"
msgstr "A&fsluiten\tCtrl+Q"

#. TRANSLATORS: Status bar help for the Exit menu item
msgid "Exit"
msgstr "Afsluiten"

#. TRANSLATORS: Help menu item opening the user guide in the web browser; the text after the tab is the keyboard shortcut
msgid "View Help in &Browser\tF1"
msgstr "Help bekijken in &browser\tF1"

#. TRANSLATORS: Status bar help for the View Help in Browser menu item
msgid "Open the user guide in your web browser"
msgstr "De handleiding openen in je webbrowser"

#. TRANSLATORS: Help menu item
msgid "Check for &Updates..."
msgstr "Controleren op &updates..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Status bar help for the Check for Updates menu item
msgid "Check for a new version of Dictymus"
msgstr "Controleren op een nieuwe versie van Dictymus"

#. TRANSLATORS: Help menu item
msgid "&About Dictymus"
msgstr "&Over Dictymus"

#. TRANSLATORS: Status bar help for the About menu item
msgid "About this application"
msgstr "Over deze toepassing"

#. TRANSLATORS: Menu bar title
msgid "&File"
msgstr "&Bestand"

#. TRANSLATORS: Menu bar title
msgid "&Help"
msgstr "&Help"

#. TRANSLATORS: Title of the Options dialog
msgid "Options"
msgstr "Opties"

#. TRANSLATORS: Label of the language selector in the Options dialog
msgid "&Language:"
msgstr "&Taal:"

#. TRANSLATORS: First entry of the language selector: follow the Windows display language
msgid "System default"
msgstr "Systeemstandaard"

#. TRANSLATORS: Option in the Options dialog
msgid "Check for &updates on startup"
msgstr "Bij het opstarten controleren op &updates"

#. TRANSLATORS: Label of the update channel selector in the Options dialog
msgid "Update &channel:"
msgstr "Update&kanaal:"

#. TRANSLATORS: Update channel entry: tagged releases only
msgid "Stable"
msgstr "Stabiel"

#. TRANSLATORS: Update channel entry: rolling development builds
msgid "Development"
msgstr "Ontwikkeling"

#. TRANSLATORS: Group label in the Options dialog around braille display settings
msgid "Braille"
msgstr "Braille"

#. TRANSLATORS: Option in the Options dialog; shows Hebrew script as ASCII braille
msgid "Show Hebrew as ASCII &braille"
msgstr "Hebreeuws als He&Braille tonen"

#. TRANSLATORS: Label for the confirmation button
#. TRANSLATORS: OK button in the Set Shortcut dialog that accepts the captured key combination.
#. TRANSLATORS: OK button that saves the customized shortcuts in the Keyboard Shortcuts dialog.
msgid "OK"
msgstr "OK"

#. TRANSLATORS: Label for the cancellation button
msgid "Cancel"
msgstr "Annuleren"

#. TRANSLATORS: Error dialog text; the placeholder is the underlying error
msgid "Could not save settings: {}"
msgstr "Kan instellingen niet opslaan: {}"

#. TRANSLATORS: Shown after changing the language in the Options dialog
msgid "The language change will take full effect after you restart Dictymus."
msgstr "De taalwijziging wordt volledig van kracht nadat Dictymus opnieuw is gestart."

#. TRANSLATORS: Announced after a search; the placeholder is the number of matching entries
msgid "{} result"
msgid_plural "{} results"
msgstr[0] "{} resultaat"
msgstr[1] "{} resultaten"

#. TRANSLATORS: Error dialog text for a protected dictionary without an installed license; the placeholder is the dictionary name
msgid "{} requires a license. Use File → Licenses... to import your license file."
msgstr "{} vereist een licentie. Gebruik Bestand → Licenties... om je licentiebestand te importeren."

#. TRANSLATORS: Label of the search field
msgid "Search"
msgstr "Zoeken"

#. TRANSLATORS: Label of the list of dictionary entries
msgid "Lemmas"
msgstr "Lemma's"

#. TRANSLATORS: Header of the single column in the list of dictionary entries
msgid "Lemma"
msgstr "Lemma"

#. TRANSLATORS: Error dialog text; first placeholder is the file path, second the underlying error
msgid "Cannot open {}: {}"
msgstr "Kan {} niet openen: {}"

#. TRANSLATORS: Announced after closing a tab; the placeholder is the dictionary title
msgid "Closed {}"
msgstr "{} gesloten"

#. TRANSLATORS: Startup warning; first placeholder is the settings file path, second the OS error.
msgid "Could not read settings ({}): {}"
msgstr "Kan instellingen niet lezen ({}): {}"

#. TRANSLATORS: Startup warning; first placeholder is the settings file path, second the parse error.
msgid "Settings file is invalid ({}): {}"
msgstr "Instellingenbestand is ongeldig ({}): {}"

msgid "Not running from an AppImage; cannot self-update."
msgstr "Draait niet vanuit een AppImage; zichzelf bijwerken is niet mogelijk."

msgid "Failed to get current exe path"
msgstr "Ophalen van huidig exe-pad mislukt"

msgid "Failed to launch update script"
msgstr "Updatescript starten mislukt"

msgid "Failed to start installation"
msgstr "Installatie starten mislukt"

msgid "Failed to stage the application"
msgstr "Applicatie voorbereiden mislukt"

msgid "The update contains a different application."
msgstr "De update bevat een andere applicatie."

msgid "Could not determine the update log directory."
msgstr "De map van het updatelogboek kon niet worden bepaald."

msgid "Failed to launch update helper"
msgstr "Updatehulpprogramma starten mislukt"

msgid "The update helper did not start. See the log:"
msgstr "Het updatehulpprogramma is niet gestart. Zie het logboek:"

msgid "The application did not quit within 60 seconds. The current app was kept."
msgstr "De applicatie is niet binnen 60 seconden afgesloten. De huidige applicatie is behouden."

msgid "The installation changed while waiting. The current app was kept."
msgstr "De installatie is tijdens het wachten gewijzigd. De huidige applicatie is behouden."

msgid "Could not move the current application. The current app was kept."
msgstr "De huidige applicatie kon niet worden verplaatst en is behouden."

msgid "Could not install the update. The previous version was restored."
msgstr "De update kon niet worden geïnstalleerd. De vorige versie is hersteld."

msgid "Could not restore the previous version. Recover it from:"
msgstr "De vorige versie kon niet worden hersteld. Herstel deze vanuit:"

msgid "macOS could not launch the update. The previous version is preserved at:"
msgstr "macOS kon de update niet starten. De vorige versie is bewaard in:"

msgid "Application update failed"
msgstr "Applicatie-update mislukt"

msgid "Log:"
msgstr "Logboek:"

msgid "Update cancelled."
msgstr "Update geannuleerd."

msgid "Failed to open disk image"
msgstr "Schijfkopie openen mislukt"

msgid "The update has been downloaded and its disk image opened. Quit %s and drag the new version into Applications to finish installing."
msgstr "De update is gedownload en de schijfkopie is geopend. Sluit %s af en sleep de nieuwe versie naar Programma's om de installatie te voltooien."

msgid "Invalid application metadata"
msgstr "Ongeldige metagegevens van applicatie"

msgid "The disk image must contain exactly one matching application."
msgstr "De schijfkopie moet precies één overeenkomende applicatie bevatten."

msgid "The update must be signed by the application's developer team"
msgstr "De update moet zijn ondertekend door het ontwikkelaarsteam van de applicatie"

msgid "Invalid application executable."
msgstr "Ongeldig uitvoerbaar bestand van applicatie."

msgid "Invalid application executable"
msgstr "Ongeldig uitvoerbaar bestand van applicatie"

msgid "Application signature verification failed"
msgstr "Verificatie van applicatiehandtekening mislukt"

msgid "Failed to mount disk image"
msgstr "Schijfkopie activeren mislukt"

msgid "Failed to unmount disk image"
msgstr "Schijfkopie deactiveren mislukt"

msgid ""
"Update downloaded to: %s\n"
"Please install it manually."
msgstr ""
"Update gedownload naar: %s\n"
"Installeer deze handmatig."

msgid "Update to %s"
msgstr "Bijwerken naar %s"

msgid "A new version of %s is available. Here's what's new:"
msgstr "Een nieuwe versie van %s is beschikbaar. Dit is er nieuw:"

#. TRANSLATORS: Label for the confirmation dialog "Yes" button
msgid "&Yes"
msgstr "&Ja"

#. TRANSLATORS: Label for the confirmation dialog "No" button
msgid "&No"
msgstr "&Nee"

msgid "No release notes provided."
msgstr "Geen releaseopmerkingen beschikbaar."

msgid "%s Update"
msgstr "%s-update"

msgid "Downloading update..."
msgstr "Update downloaden..."

msgid "Update failed"
msgstr "Update mislukt"

msgid "Preparing update..."
msgstr "Update voorbereiden..."

msgid "Error"
msgstr "Fout"

msgid "Update Ready"
msgstr "Update gereed"

msgid "No updates available."
msgstr "Geen updates beschikbaar."

msgid "No updates available. Latest version: %s"
msgstr "Geen updates beschikbaar. Nieuwste versie: %s"

msgid "Info"
msgstr "Info"

msgid "Security verification failed. The update might have been tampered with: %s"
msgstr "Veiligheidsverificatie mislukt. Mogelijk is met de update geknoeid: %s"

msgid "Security Error"
msgstr "Veiligheidsfout"

#. TRANSLATORS: Duration segment for hours (for example, "1 hour" or "5 hours"). The %d placeholder is replaced with the count.
msgid "%d hour"
msgid_plural "%d hours"
msgstr[0] "%d uur"
msgstr[1] "%d uur"

#. TRANSLATORS: Duration segment for minutes (for example, "1 minute" or "5 minutes"). The %d placeholder is replaced with the count.
msgid "%d minute"
msgid_plural "%d minutes"
msgstr[0] "%d minuut"
msgstr[1] "%d minuten"

#. TRANSLATORS: Duration segment for seconds (for example, "1 second" or "5 seconds"). The %d placeholder is replaced with the count.
msgid "%d second"
msgid_plural "%d seconds"
msgstr[0] "%d seconde"
msgstr[1] "%d seconden"

#. TRANSLATORS: Title of the Set Shortcut dialog. The {} placeholder is replaced with the action's display name.
msgid "Set Shortcut for {}"
msgstr "Sneltoets instellen voor {}"

#. TRANSLATORS: Instruction text in the Set Shortcut dialog. The {} placeholder is replaced with the action's display name.
msgid "Configure shortcut for {}:"
msgstr "Sneltoets configureren voor {}:"

#. TRANSLATORS: Checkbox in the Set Shortcut dialog that includes the Command modifier in the shortcut, on macOS.
msgid "&Cmd"
msgstr "&Cmd"

#. TRANSLATORS: Checkbox in the Set Shortcut dialog that includes the Option modifier in the shortcut, on macOS.
msgid "&Option"
msgstr "&Option"

#. TRANSLATORS: Checkbox in the Set Shortcut dialog that includes the Ctrl modifier in the shortcut.
msgid "&Ctrl"
msgstr "&Ctrl"

#. TRANSLATORS: Checkbox in the Set Shortcut dialog that includes the Alt modifier in the shortcut.
msgid "&Alt"
msgstr "&Alt"

#. TRANSLATORS: Checkbox in the Set Shortcut dialog that includes the Shift modifier in the shortcut.
msgid "&Shift"
msgstr "&Shift"

#. TRANSLATORS: Checkbox in the Set Shortcut dialog that includes the Windows logo key in a system-wide shortcut.
msgid "&Win"
msgstr "&Win"

#. TRANSLATORS: Label next to the key field in the Set Shortcut dialog.
msgid "&Key:"
msgstr "&Toets:"

msgid "Tip: click in the key field and press the key combination you want."
msgstr "Tip: klik in het toetsveld en druk op de gewenste toetsencombinatie."

#. TRANSLATORS: Placeholder shown in the Set Shortcut dialog before any key combination has been captured
msgid "Detected: (none)"
msgstr "Gedetecteerd: (geen)"

msgid "Detected: {}"
msgstr "Gedetecteerd: {}"

msgid "No key detected"
msgstr "Geen toets gedetecteerd"

#. TRANSLATORS: Button in the Set Shortcut dialog that clears the captured key combination.
msgid "&Clear"
msgstr "&Wissen"

#. TRANSLATORS: Title of the Keyboard Shortcuts dialog.
msgid "Customize Keyboard Shortcuts"
msgstr "Toetsenbordsneltoetsen aanpassen"

#. TRANSLATORS: Label above the list of shortcuts for a tab in the Keyboard Shortcuts dialog.
msgid "&Shortcuts:"
msgstr "&Sneltoetsen:"

#. TRANSLATORS: Button in the Keyboard Shortcuts dialog that opens a prompt to assign a new shortcut to the selected action.
msgid "&Set Shortcut..."
msgstr "Sneltoets &instellen..."

#. TRANSLATORS: Button in the Keyboard Shortcuts dialog that removes the shortcut assigned to the selected action.
msgid "&Clear Shortcut"
msgstr "Sneltoets &wissen"

#. TRANSLATORS: Button in the Keyboard Shortcuts dialog that restores the selected action's shortcut to its default.
msgid "&Reset to Default"
msgstr "&Herstellen naar standaardwaarden"

#. TRANSLATORS: Button in the Keyboard Shortcuts dialog that restores every action's shortcut to its default.
msgid "Reset &All to Defaults"
msgstr "&Alles herstellen naar standaardwaarden"

msgid "A system-wide shortcut needs Ctrl, Alt, or Win, or it would take that key from every other program."
msgstr "Een systeembrede sneltoets moet Ctrl, Alt of Win bevatten, anders kunnen alle andere programma's die toets niet meer gebruiken."

#. TRANSLATORS: Title of the dialog refusing a shortcut that can't be used.
msgid "Shortcut Not Allowed"
msgstr "Sneltoets niet toegestaan"

#. TRANSLATORS: the three {} are, in order: the key chord, the action it's currently assigned to, and the action being (re)assigned to it
msgid "'{}' is already assigned to '{}'. Reassign it to '{}'?"
msgstr "'{}' is al toegewezen aan '{}'. Opnieuw toewijzen aan '{}'?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Title of the dialog warning that a shortcut is already taken
msgid "Shortcut Conflict"
msgstr "Sneltoetsconflict"

#. TRANSLATORS: Confirmation prompt shown when resetting keyboard shortcuts that span more than one tab to their defaults.
msgid "Reset all shortcuts to their default values?"
msgstr "Alle sneltoetsen naar de standaardwaarden herstellen?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Confirmation prompt shown when resetting the current tab's keyboard shortcuts to their defaults.
msgid "Reset all shortcuts in this tab to their default values?"
msgstr "Alle sneltoetsen op dit tabblad naar de standaardwaarden herstellen?"

#. TRANSLATORS: Title of the confirmation dialog for resetting keyboard shortcuts to their defaults.
msgid "Reset Shortcuts"
msgstr "Sneltoetsen herstellen"

msgid "None"
msgstr "Geen"

#. TRANSLATORS: A shortcut in the Customize Keyboard Shortcuts list whose key is not on the keyboard layout in use, so it cannot be pressed. The {} placeholder is replaced with the shortcut, for example "Ctrl+;".
msgid "{} (not on this keyboard layout)"
msgstr "{} (niet op deze toetsenbordindeling)"
